  "derivation": "Source glTF positions/normals transformed back to authored local runtime axes (x,-z,y). For each of six axis-normal faces, solve affine source face UV using positions, verify max residual <1e-6, then use its four plane bounds; end-cap rectangles inset 2mm on both plane axes to stay inside the source chamfer octagon. Store 24 UVs per source member on material metadata; runtime unit boxes retain their existing six quads, winding, transforms and dimensions. Source chamfer geometry and source-only 105mm board extension are not incorporated. No metric UV is applied to this atlas. All three embedded atlas image byte sequences remain unchanged. Runtime shader pigment is separate: only green member roles receive the linear per-lot colour ratio through CUSTOM0 RGBFloat; pale cap roles retain identity.",
  "source_material_roles": {
    "Source_7f9a74_wood_painted_trim": "green posts, bearing rails and pickets",
    "Source_e3d6b8_wood_painted_trim": "warm pale cap rail",
    "Source_e6dfc6_wood_painted_trim": "warm pale post caps"
  },
  "batching": "One additional family mesh with one atlas ShaderMaterial/surface, calculated +1 surface (within +1..+3 budget); no runtime performance or FPS measurement. Gates/wickets and other families keep their existing material batches. CUSTOM0 RGBFloat adds 12 bytes per indexed vertex (288 bytes per isolated six-quad box, 432 bytes per unindexed construction box); no additional texture or draw surface per lot colour.",
  "review": "Source/candidate front-right views and albedo atlas visually inspected 2026-10-27; village scene, motion, native texture import and cultural acceptance remain open.",
